<h2>Find repeated text across pages</h2><p class="lead">Compare pasted page text, identify exact duplicate blocks and measure similarity without uploading your content.</p>
<div class="field full"><label for="pageText">Page content — one page per section</label><textarea id="pageText" style="min-height:260px" placeholder="PAGE 1\nPaste the visible text from page one here...\n\n--- PAGE BREAK ---\n\nPAGE 2\nPaste the visible text from page two here..."></textarea><small>Use the marker <code>--- PAGE BREAK ---</code> to compare multiple pages. For best results, paste main content rather than navigation, footer or cookie text.</small></div>
<div class="form-grid"><div class="field"><label for="minWords">Minimum repeated phrase</label><select id="minWords"><option value="3">3 words</option><option value="4" selected>4 words</option><option value="5">5 words</option><option value="6">6 words</option></select></div><div class="field"><label for="maxPhrases">Maximum phrase matches</label><select id="maxPhrases"><option value="20">20</option><option value="40" selected>40</option><option value="80">80</option></select></div></div>
<div class="tool-actions"><button class="btn btn-primary" id="analyze" type="button">Find duplicates</button><button class="btn btn-secondary" id="copy" type="button">Copy report</button></div><div class="result-box" id="result" hidden aria-live="polite"><div class="result-grid"><div class="metric"><span>Pages compared</span><strong id="pages">0</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Repeated phrases</span><strong id="phraseCount">0</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Highest similarity</span><strong id="highest">—</strong></div></div><h3>Page-pair similarity</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Page A</th><th>Page B</th><th>Shared words</th><th>Similarity</th></tr></thead><tbody id="pairs"></tbody></table></div><h3>Repeated exact phrases</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Phrase</th><th>Pages</th><th>Coverage</th></tr></thead><tbody id="phrases"></tbody></table></div><div class="notice"><strong>Interpretation:</strong> High text overlap is a review signal. It does not prove a search engine will treat pages as duplicates, because canonicalization and other page-level signals also matter. citeturn112108search3</div></div>
<script>(()=>{const $=i=>document.getElementById(i);const esc=s=>String(s??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#039;'}[c]));const toks=s=>(s.toLowerCase().match(/[\p{L}\p{N}]+(?:['’-][\p{L}\p{N}]+)*/gu)||[]);function sets(a){return new Set(a)}function similarity(a,b){const A=sets(a),B=sets(b);let inter=0;A.forEach(x=>{if(B.has(x))inter++});const union=new Set([...A,...B]).size;return union?inter/union:0}function phraseMap(words,n){const m=new Map();for(let i=0;i<=words.length-n;i++){const p=words.slice(i,i+n).join(' ');m.set(p,(m.get(p)||0)+1)}return m}function go(){const raw=$('pageText').value.split(/\n\s*---\s*PAGE BREAK\s*---\s*\n/i).map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean);const pages=raw.map(toks);$('pages').textContent=pages.length;const pairRows=[];let high=0;for(let i=0;i<pages.length;i++){for(let j=i+1;j<pages.length;j++){const sim=similarity(pages[i],pages[j]);high=Math.max(high,sim);const shared=[...sets(pages[i])].filter(x=>sets(pages[j]).has(x)).length;pairRows.push([i+1,j+1,shared,sim])}}$('pairs').innerHTML=pairRows.length?pairRows.sort((a,b)=>b[3]-a[3]).map(r=>`<tr><td>${r[0]}</td><td>${r[1]}</td><td>${r[2]}</td><td>${(r[3]*100).toFixed(1)}%</td></tr>`).join(''):'<tr><td colspan="4">Add at least two pages using the page-break marker.</td></tr>';$('highest').textContent=pairRows.length?(high*100).toFixed(1)+'%':'—';const n=Number($('minWords').value),limit=Number($('maxPhrases').value),all=new Map();pages.forEach((w,idx)=>{phraseMap(w,n).forEach((count,p)=>{if(!all.has(p))all.set(p,new Set());all.get(p).add(idx)})});const repeated=[...all.entries()].filter(([,s])=>s.size>1).sort((a,b)=>b[1].size-a[1].size||a[0].localeCompare(b[0])).slice(0,limit);$('phraseCount').textContent=repeated.length;$('phrases').innerHTML=repeated.length?repeated.map(([p,s])=>`<tr><td>${esc(p)}</td><td>${[...s].map(x=>x+1).join(', ')}</td><td>${s.size}/${pages.length}</td></tr>`).join(''):'<tr><td colspan="3">No repeated phrases of the selected length were found.</td></tr>';$('result').hidden=false;window._dupReport=[`Pages compared: ${pages.length}`,`Highest Jaccard word-set similarity: ${(high*100).toFixed(1)}%`,`Repeated ${n}-word phrase matches: ${repeated.length}`,`Top pair matches: ${pairRows.slice(0,10).map(r=>`Page ${r[0]} + Page ${r[1]} ${(r[3]*100).toFixed(1)}%`).join(' | ')||'None'}`].join('\n')}$('analyze').onclick=go;$('copy').onclick=()=>{if(window._dupReport)tkCopy(window._dupReport)};})();</script>
<?php $toolBody=ob_get_clean();ob_start(); ?>
<h2>What this duplicate content finder measures</h2><p>The tool compares the unique word sets of each pasted page pair using Jaccard similarity, then looks for exact repeated phrases across pages. It is a local content-review aid, not a search-engine duplication detector.</p>
<h2>How to use it</h2><ol><li>Paste each page's main text into its own section.</li><li>Separate pages with <code>--- PAGE BREAK ---</code>.</li><li>Choose the minimum phrase length and run the analysis.</li><li>Review high-overlap page pairs and repeated phrases before deciding whether pages need rewriting, consolidation, or a canonical strategy.</li></ol>
<h2>Why similarity is only a signal</h2><p>Search engines can cluster substantially similar URLs and choose a canonical based on several signals. Similarity in this tool does not reproduce that process and should not be treated as a pass/fail SEO score. citeturn112108search3</p>
<h2>Reduce false positives</h2><p>Shared navigation, legal notices, product boilerplate and template text can make unrelated pages look similar. Paste the main content when possible. Compare pages that serve different search intents separately from pages that intentionally reuse the same standard copy.</p>
<?php $toolContent=ob_get_clean();$faqs=[['Does this tool check live website URLs?','No. It compares text pasted into the browser, so the page content stays local in this version.'],['Does high similarity prove Google sees duplicate content?','No. It is a review signal. Search engines use multiple page-level signals when clustering and selecting canonical URLs.'],['What similarity formula is used?','The page-pair percentage is Jaccard similarity over unique detected words: shared unique words divided by the union of unique words.'],['Can I compare more than two pages?','Yes. Add multiple sections separated by the --- PAGE BREAK --- marker, then the tool compares every page pair.']];require __DIR__.'/../includes/tool-template.php';